A few structural notes:

Every chapter should end with a "Quick Recap" and a "Try It Yourself" exercise — this keeps it hands-on throughout.
The FAQ and Pitfalls sections inside each part are the secret weapon — they're what make this book stand out from official docs.
Part 7's projects are what turn readers from learners into practitioners. Don't skip these.
Since it's Markdown on GitHub, each Part can be a folder with one .md file per chapter — easy for contributors to pick up individual chapters.
